<% --[[ The workspace rail: categories down the left, each one opening in place.

        It is a column of icons until the pointer reaches it, and then it widens and puts a name
        beside every icon. Clicking a category unfolds its tools underneath, where the rest of the
        rail stays visible around them. The alternative, a panel flying out beside the icon under the
        cursor, showed one category at a time and hid the shape of everything else.

        `<details>` rather than a class we would have to toggle: the browser already owns "this is
        open", the state survives the rail being swapped after a navigation, and `name` makes the set
        exclusive without a line of script. The category you are inside is open on arrival, which is
        the only default anyone would have chosen by hand.

        Nothing here is a list this file knows. Categories and tools are collected from whoever
        contributed them, so a category arrives by a module being present and leaves by it being
        removed. A category with no tools is not drawn: an empty section is a promise, and the rail
        is meant to be read at a glance. ]] %>
<aside class="workrail" id="workrail"<% if oob then %> hx-swap-oob="true"<% end %>>
  <nav>
    <a class="wcat one<%= active == "overview" and " on" or "" %>" href="/workspace">
      <span class="wico"><%- icon("layout-dashboard") %></span>
      <span class="wlabel">Overview</span>
    </a>

    <% if #cats > 0 then %><span class="wsep"></span><% end %>

    <% for _, c in ipairs(cats) do %>
      <details class="wcat<%= c.on and " on" or "" %>" name="wcat"<% if c.on then %> open<% end %>>
        <summary>
          <span class="wico"><%- icon(c.icon) %></span>
          <span class="wlabel"><%= c.name %></span>
          <span class="wchev"><%- icon("chevron-right") %></span>
        </summary>

        <div class="wtools">
          <% if c.blurb then %><span class="wblurb"><%= c.blurb %></span><% end %>

          <% for _, t in ipairs(c.tools) do %>
            <% if t.path then %>
              <a class="wtool<%= t.on and " on" or "" %>" href="<%= t.path %>">
                <span><%= t.name %></span>
                <% --[[ The tool declared that it writes. Said in the rail as well as on the tool's
                        own page, because the moment to know is before the click. ]] %>
                <% if t.writes then %><span class="pen" title="Writes to the target"><%-
                   icon("pencil") %></span><% end %>
              </a>
            <% else %>
              <% --[[ Deliberately not a link. A page that only says "not built yet" is a click that
                      cost you your place, and six of them is what this rail replaced. ]] %>
              <span class="wtool off">
                <span><%= t.name %></span>
                <em class="soon">planned</em>
              </span>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </details>
    <% end %>
  </nav>
</aside>
